{"decision": "edit", "issues": [{"quote": "The nearer mass appears smooth and reflective overall.", "problem": "In the early frames the foreground mass has a distinct angular upper crest and faceted surfaces, so describing it as smooth overall misstates its visible appearance."}, {"quote": "the bowls remain fixed in position relative to the camera throughout the visible excerpt.", "problem": "This is an absolute stillness claim; the visible sequence supports that the bowls stay largely in place, not that they are fixed throughout."}], "caption": "The video captures two white ceramic bowls decorated with purple and pink floral rims resting on a wooden surface beside a window. The nearer bowl contains a large glossy translucent mass with an angular upper crest, while the farther bowl holds a similar pale solid. A greenish cast falls across the left edge in view, and the bowls stay largely in place relative to the camera. The nearer mass is glossy, reflective, and faceted.

Over time, the upper-left corner of the foreground mass loses its sharp edge and rounds downward. The solid slumps into a lower, smoother form, and a wet sheen becomes more apparent across the lower interior of the bowl. The background mass shows only slight deformation, remaining largely in place.

The change is not a shift of the bowls or the masses across the scene, but a deformation inside each bowl. The foreground solid continues to soften its contours, with the angular crest becoming part of a rounded surface. The farther pale form similarly adjusts without leaving its dish.", "length_note": ""}
